# An experiment's evidence file is hashed in its own manifest.json, and that hash is the
# whole immutability proof the research record rests on - see research/README.md. `-text`
# keeps git from rewriting the file's line endings on checkout, which a clone with
# core.autocrlf set would otherwise do: the bytes would stop matching the recorded hash,
# and the proof would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the run. Scoped to
# that one path, so every other file in the repository keeps git's ordinary handling.
research/experiments/*/body-events.jsonl -text
